---
/**
 * Compound interest calculator — 싱가포르판 세 번째 도구. 한국어판 /tools/compound/ 와 계산(lib/compound.ts)·스크립트를 같이 쓰고
 * (문구는 scripts/compound.ts 의 EN 사전, 통화는 판의 SGD·en-SG), 문장은 싱가포르 영어로 새로 썼다(번역 아님).
 * 복리 산술이라 rates 와 상관없다(조사표 싱가포르 칸 '같음').
 *
 * 소제목은 싱가포르 구글 자동완성에서 왔다(keywords/sg-compound-2026-10-21.csv, hl en · gl sg):
 *   compound interest calculator sgd · monthly deposit · monthly contributions / is there a formula for calculating compound interest /
 *   how much to save per month singapore · monthly savings calculator singapore / savings account calculator singapore ·
 *   savings interest calculator singapore / compound interest calculator cpf · savings calculator cpf
 * 세율 기본값은 0% — 한국어판 15.4% 는 한국 원천징수라 쓰지 않는다. 싱가포르 쪽 사실은 IRAS 원문에서 확인한 것만:
 *   approved banks in Singapore·licensed finance companies 예금 이자는 non-taxable, non-approved·unlicensed 쪽은 taxable
 *   (https://www.iras.gov.sg/taxes/individual-income-tax/basics-of-individual-income-tax/what-is-taxable-what-is-not/interest,
 *   Last updated 15 October 2026, 확인 2026-10-21). CPF 이자율 숫자는 확인하지 않아 쓰지 않는다.
 * 본문 숫자는 전부 아래 frontmatter 에서 compound() 로 계산한다.
 */
import BaseHead from "../../../../components/BaseHead.astro";
import AdSlot from "../../../../components/AdSlot.astro";
import ClarityHead from "../../../../components/ClarityHead.astro";
import GtagHead from "../../../../components/GtagHead.astro";
import TrackLinks from "../../../../components/TrackLinks.astro";
import AdSenseHead from "../../../../components/AdSenseHead.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { compound } from "../../../../lib/compound";
import "../../../../styles/global.css";

const title = "Compound Interest Calculator Singapore (SGD) — Monthly Deposits, Formula, Savings Goal";
const description =
  "Singapore compound interest calculator in SGD: a starting sum plus monthly deposits, interest earned, monthly saving for a goal, inflation and Excel FV.";

const base = { principal: 10_000, monthly: 500, ratePct: 3, months: 120, taxPct: 0, inflationPct: 0 };
const ex = compound({ ...base, timing: "start" });
const exEnd = compound({ ...base, timing: "end" });
const lump = compound({ ...base, monthly: 0, timing: "start" });
const onlyMonthly = compound({ ...base, principal: 0, timing: "start" });
const real2 = compound({ ...base, timing: "start", inflationPct: 2 });
const higher = compound({ ...base, monthly: 800, timing: "start" });
const sgd = (x: number) =>
  Math.round(x).toLocaleString("en-SG", { style: "currency", currency: "SGD", maximumFractionDigits: 0, minimumFractionDigits: 0 });
---

<html lang="en-SG">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
    <ClarityHead />
    <GtagHead />
    <AdSenseHead />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-texture">
    <SiteHeader />
    <main>
      <h1>Compound Interest Calculator (SGD)</h1>
      <p>
        Key in a starting sum, how much you put aside every month and an interest rate per year. The calculator adds interest
        monthly and shows your ending balance in Singapore dollars, split into your own deposits and the interest earned. The rate,
        tax and inflation you enter are your own assumptions — the result is not a quote from any bank, insurer or CPF account.
      </p>

      <div class="calc-card" data-two>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="cp-principal">Starting sum ($)</label>
          <input type="text" inputmode="numeric" id="cp-principal" value="10,000" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="cp-monthly">Monthly deposit ($)</label>
          <input type="text" inputmode="numeric" id="cp-monthly" value="500" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="cp-rate">Interest rate or return per year</label>
          <input type="number" id="cp-rate" value="3" min="-50" max="100" step="0.1" inputmode="decimal" />
          <span class="unit">%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="cp-period">Period</label>
          <input type="number" id="cp-period" value="10" min="1" max="600" step="1" data-step />
          <select id="cp-unit" aria-label="Time unit">
            <option value="years" selected>years</option>
            <option value="months">months</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="cp-timing">When you deposit</label>
          <select id="cp-timing" data-seg>
            <option value="start" selected>Start of each month</option>
            <option value="end">End of each month</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="cp-tax">Tax on the interest (assumption)</label>
          <input type="number" id="cp-tax" value="0" min="0" max="100" step="0.001" inputmode="decimal" />
          <span class="unit">%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="cp-infl">Inflation per year</label>
          <input type="number" id="cp-infl" value="0" min="-20" max="50" step="0.1" inputmode="decimal" />
          <span class="unit">%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="cp-goal">Savings goal ($, optional)</label>
          <input type="text" inputmode="numeric" id="cp-goal" value="" placeholder="e.g. 100,000" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>

        <div
          class="result-hero"
          aria-live="polite"
          aria-atomic="true"
          data-bar="cp-paid|cp-gain2"
          data-bar-labels="Deposits|Interest"
          data-dock="cp-hero"
        >
          <p class="label">Ending balance (before tax)</p>
          <p class="big" id="cp-hero">{sgd(ex.balance)}</p>
          <p class="meta" id="cp-note">120 months · 0.25% a month · deposits at the start of each month</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-row" data-receipt>
          <div class="stat-chip"><span class="label">Total deposits</span><span class="value" id="cp-paid">{sgd(ex.paid)}</span></div>
          <div class="stat-chip"><span class="label">Interest earned</span><span class="value" id="cp-gain2">{sgd(ex.gain)}</span></div>
          <div class="stat-chip"><span class="label">Tax (assumed)</span><span class="value" id="cp-tax-v">$0</span></div>
          <div class="stat-chip"><span class="label">After tax</span><span class="value" id="cp-after">{sgd(ex.afterTax)}</span></div>
          <div class="stat-chip"><span class="label">In today's dollars</span><span class="value" id="cp-real">{sgd(ex.real)}</span></div>
          <div class="stat-chip"><span class="label">Goal reached</span><span class="value" id="cp-goal-v">No goal set</span></div>
        </div>

        <details>
          <summary>Year-by-year deposits, interest and balance</summary>
          <div class="table-scroll">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Period</th><th>Deposits that year</th><th>Interest that year</th><th>Balance</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody id="cp-rows">
                {ex.years.map((r) => <tr><th scope="row">Year {r.year}</th><td>{sgd(r.paid)}</td><td>{sgd(r.gain)}</td><td>{sgd(r.balance)}</td></tr>)}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p class="meta">The starting sum is not counted in "Deposits that year"; it only shows up in the balance.</p>
        </details>

        <div class="actions">
          <button id="btn-download" type="button">Save as image</button>
          <button id="btn-share" type="button" class="secondary">Share</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Is there a formula for calculating compound interest?</h2>
      <p>Yes. This calculator uses monthly compounding, worked out step by step:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Monthly rate</strong> — r = yearly rate ÷ 12. At 3% a year that is 0.25% a month.</li>
        <li><strong>Deposit at the start of the month</strong> — the new money earns that month's interest: balance = (balance + deposit) × (1 + r).</li>
        <li><strong>Deposit at the end of the month</strong> — interest goes in first, then the deposit: balance = balance × (1 + r) + deposit. The last deposit earns nothing, so the total is slightly lower.</li>
        <li><strong>Closed form</strong> — after n months, FV = P(1 + r)<sup>n</sup> + PMT × [(1 + r)<sup>n</sup> − 1] ÷ r, with the PMT part multiplied by (1 + r) once more when you deposit at the start of the month. P is the starting sum and PMT the monthly deposit.</li>
        <li><strong>Tax</strong> — if you enter a tax rate, it is taken once from the gain (ending balance minus total deposits). A loss is not taxed.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Example: {sgd(base.principal)} to start and {sgd(base.monthly)} a month at 3% a year for 10 years. You put in
        {" "}{sgd(ex.paid)} and end with {sgd(ex.balance)}, so {sgd(ex.gain)} is interest. If you deposit at the end of each month
        instead, the balance is {sgd(exEnd.balance)}.
      </p>

      <h2>Compound interest with monthly deposits vs a lump sum</h2>
      <p>
        Money that is in the account from day one compounds for the full period; each monthly deposit has less time left to grow.
        In the example, the {sgd(base.principal)} starting sum on its own grows to {sgd(lump.balance)}, while the {sgd(base.monthly)}
        monthly deposits on their own grow to {sgd(onlyMonthly.balance)}. Put $0 in either box to see one part at a time.
      </p>

      <h2>How much to save per month to reach a goal</h2>
      <p>
        Type a figure into "Savings goal" and the calculator tells you after how long the balance first reaches it, or that it is not
        reached within the period. Then adjust the monthly deposit until the goal lands where you want it. For example, raising the
        deposit from {sgd(base.monthly)} to {sgd(800)} a month (same {sgd(base.principal)} start, 3%, 10 years) lifts the ending balance
        from {sgd(ex.balance)} to {sgd(higher.balance)}.
      </p>

      <h2>Savings account interest and inflation</h2>
      <p>
        A savings account may pay different rates on different balance tiers or only when you meet conditions, and rates can change.
        This calculator uses one flat rate for the whole period, so treat the result as a what-if, not as your bank's figure. "In
        today's dollars" divides the after-tax balance by (1 + inflation)<sup>years</sup>: at 2% inflation the example's
        {" "}{sgd(ex.balance)} is worth about {sgd(real2.real)} in today's money.
      </p>

      <h2>Compound interest in Excel or Google Sheets</h2>
      <p>
        The FV function gives the same result. For deposits at the start of each month use
        <code>=FV(3%/12, 120, -500, -10000, 1)</code>; for the end of the month change the last 1 to 0. The deposit and starting sum are
        negative because they are money going out of your pocket.
      </p>

      <details>
        <summary>Do I pay tax on bank interest in Singapore?</summary>
        <p>
          IRAS lists interest from deposits with approved banks in Singapore and with finance companies licensed in Singapore as
          non-taxable, while interest from non-approved banks or unlicensed finance companies is taxable. That is why the tax box starts at 0% — enter a rate only if your interest is taxable
          (<a href="https://www.iras.gov.sg/taxes/individual-income-tax/basics-of-individual-income-tax/what-is-taxable-what-is-not/interest" rel="noopener" target="_blank">IRAS: Interest</a>,
          last updated 15 October 2026, checked 21 October 2026).
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I use it as a CPF compound interest calculator?</summary>
        <p>
          Only as a rough picture of growth at a rate you choose. CPF accounts earn interest under their own rules set by the CPF
          Board, which this calculator does not model, and no CPF rate is filled in here. For your actual CPF balances and
          projections, use the calculators on <a href="https://www.cpf.gov.sg/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">cpf.gov.sg</a>.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is this the same as simple interest?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Simple interest is calculated on the starting amount only; compound interest also earns on interest already added. For
          a product that pays simple interest, the figure here will be higher than what you actually receive.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I enter cents or a $ sign?</summary>
        <p>
          Amounts are whole dollars. A typed $ sign and commas are ignored, but a decimal point is not read as cents — enter 1500
          rather than 1,500.50.
        </p>
      </details>

      <AdSlot label="compound-result-en-sg" />
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
    <script src="../../../../scripts/compound.ts"></script>
    <TrackLinks />
    <script src="../../../../scripts/calc-ui.ts"></script>
  </body>
</html>
